ople were cautious about travel, were typically day trips.", "id": "1298779687766949889"}, {"response": "Option: 3. more than 30 days.\n\nThe tweet is from SOTA (Student Occupational Therapy Association) at UTRGV (University of Texas Rio Grande Valley) in Edinburg, TX. This is announcing the start of the fall semester for 2nd year occupational therapy students. Since this is posted by what appears to be an official university account about students beginning a semester, they would typically stay for the entire academic term. A fall semester typically lasts 3-4 months (more than 30 days), and since these are 2nd year students in a professional program, they are likely to remain at the university for the full semester and beyond. The image shows students in a classroom setting with COVID precautions (masks, social distancing), suggesting they are settled in for regular classes throughout the semester.", "id": "1298788521352847361"}, {"response": "Option: 3. more than 30 days.\n\nReason: The tweet was posted from San Antonio, TX on August 26, 2020, during the COVID-19 pandemic. The content of the tweet references being \"stuck in #quarantine\" and discusses press-on nails supplies, suggesting the person is a resident of San Antonio rather than a visitor. The tweet shows nail supplies/stands and mentions nail-related hashtags, indicating this is likely their home and business location. There's no indication of travel or temporary stay - instead, the context suggests they are a local nail technician dealing with quarantine restrictions while continuing their business. Given the date during the pandemic and the established business context, they are most likely staying in San Antonio for more than 30 days.", "id": "1298830470784995329"}, {"response": "Option: 1. less than 24 hours.\n\nReason: The tweet is about a tattoo that was done by an artist named lloguell at what appears to be a tattoo shop in Randolph, NJ. The image shows a black and grey plague doctor tattoo. This suggests the person was visiting the tattoo shop specifically to get this tattoo done, which is typically a procedure that takes only a few hours. There's no indication that the person lives in or is staying in Randolph - they likely just visited the tattoo shop for their appointment and would leave afterward. Getting a tattoo is usually a single-day activity, so they would likely stay in Randolph for less than 24 hours.", "id": "1299054631645978629"}, {"response": "Option: 2. 1-30 days.\n\nReason: The tweet was posted from Las Vegas, NV on August 27, 2020, during the COVID-19 pandemic. The person is sharing positive vibes with a Bob Marley quote and using hashtags like #Quarantine and #Positivity. While they're in Las Vegas (likely for tourism or a visit), there's no specific indication they're permanently relocating there. The image shows someone posing in front of what appears to be colorful artwork, suggesting they're enjoying tourist activities. Las Vegas is typically a destination for short to medium-length visits rather than permanent relocation, especially during the pandemic when travel was limited. Therefore, a stay of 1-30 days seems most likely for this visit.", "id": "1299057917660889089"}, {"response": "Option: 1. less than 24 hours.\n\nReason: The tweet is about a visit to the Mendon drive-in theater, which is a single-day activity. The person mentions this was \"one of the few last days of #summer2020 a couple of weeks ago,\" indicating they're sharing a past experience, not announcing a current extended stay. They also mention they \"have been going to the drive-in quite a bunch this #quarantine,\" suggesting they make occasional visits to the drive-in but don't stay in Mendon. They appear to be local residents who visit the drive-in for movie screenings and then return home the same day, which typically lasts only a few hours.", "id": "1299089441340956673"}, {"response": "Option: 1. less than 24 hours.\n\nReason: The tweet is promoting a specific event at a Dairy Queen location that is happening the same day as the tweet was posted (\"Tonight 5-8pm\"). The author appears to be sharing information about a school benefit fundraiser with a defined start and end time (5-8pm). The images show the Dairy Queen sign advertising the event and people at the location wearing masks during the COVID-19 pandemic. There's no indication that the author is visiting Lincoln or planning to stay for an extended period - rather, they seem to be a local promoting a community event that will only last for 3 hours on that specific evening.", "id": "1299119171733606400"}, {"response": "Option: 3. more than 30 days.\n\nThe tweet appears to be from Teatro8, a theater group or venue in Miami, encouraging local residents to follow COVID-19 safety measures like wearing masks until the pandemic subsides. The hashtags like #MaskUpMiami, #SaveOurStages, #HispanicTheater, and #LatinTheater suggest this is a local organization addressing their community. The image shows theater masks wearing face masks with the \"#MaskUpMiami\" hashtag.\n\nThe language \"let's keep this down till it disappears from town\" indicates the author is part of the Miami community and is planning to remain there throughout the pandemic duration. Given that this was posted in August 2020 during the height of the pandemic, and the author is likely a local theater organization, they would be staying in Miami for the foreseeable future, certainly more than 30 days.", "id": "1299128177969823745"}, {"response": "Option: 3. more than 30 days.\n\nReason: The tweet shows a home office setup for broadcasting/monitoring conventions, with multiple screens and professional equipment. The hashtags #workfromhome indicates this is a long-term work arrangement during the COVID-19 pandemic (posted in August 2020). The person appears to be working professionally from home in Union County, New Jersey, suggesting this is their residence where they have established a permanent work setup.