orting local businesses. All these factors suggest the author is a resident of Baltimore rather than a visitor, meaning they would stay there for more than 30 days after posting the tweet.", "id": "1299461569617821703"}, {"response": "Option: 1. less than 24 hours.\n\nReason: The tweet appears to be promoting Biden-Harris merchandise at a specific location (Afro World Hair and Fashion Company in Normandy, MO). The content suggests the person is there for a commercial or promotional purpose, displaying campaign t-shirts, face shields, and masks for sale. This type of activity typically indicates a short visit or a day trip to sell or promote these items rather than an extended stay in Normandy. There's no indication of accommodation or longer-term plans mentioned in the tweet that would suggest the person is staying in the city for multiple days.", "id": "1299462905105186817"}, {"response": "Option: 3. more than 30 days.\n\nReason: The tweet is from a local business called \"The Sign & Print Machine\" located in Kapaa, Hawaii. The content shows they are manufacturing safety guideline signs related to COVID-19 protocols. The hashtags #supportlocal and #smallbusiness indicate this is their own business in this location. This appears to be a business promoting their products (A-Frame panels with safety guidelines) rather than someone visiting temporarily. As a local business owner/operator, they would be based in Kapaa for an extended period, certainly more than 30 days. They are not indicating any travel plans or temporary visit - they are operating their business from this location.", "id": "1299470760038338563"}, {"response": "Option: 3. more than 30 days.\n\nThe tweet was posted during the COVID-19 pandemic (August 28, 2020) from Bloomingdale, IL. The person is showing a product from Defense Soap and mentioning their Brazilian Jiu Jitsu Academy in the location tag. This suggests the person is at their home base where they train and teach Jiu Jitsu. The hashtags like