shows the person making face masks with custom designs. They appear to be creating these masks at home in Oak Creek, WI, as evidenced by the location tag. The content suggests this is their residence where they're engaging in a crafting project (making custom face masks with a Joker-inspired design). The hashtags #covid19 and #facemasks indicate this is part of their pandemic life, not a temporary visit. Since this appears to be their home where they're creating pandemic supplies, and not a travel destination, they would likely stay there for more than 30 days.", "id": "1299776458898968578"}, {"response": "Option: 3. more than 30 days.\n\nThe tweet indicates this is likely the person's home area rather than a temporary visit. The hashtags #sandiego, #socal, and #california suggest the author is local to San Diego. The post was made during August 2020, in the midst of the COVID-19 pandemic (as indicated by hashtags #covid19, #maskon, and #socialdistance). The author is visiting Balboa Park with their husband (hashtags #husband #lovehim) and creating memories in their local area during the pandemic (#makingmemories). The presence of hashtags related to safety during COVID and the fact they're at Ocean Beach, a residential neighborhood in San Diego, further suggests this is their home area where they will remain for an extended period rather than a short trip or vacation.", "id": "1299844338474778630"}, {"response": "Option: 3. more than 30 days.\n\nThe tweet appears to be from a local Austin artist (indicated by hashtags #atxartist and #atxgraffiti) who is sharing street art or graffiti in Austin, TX during the COVID-19 pandemic. The date shows August 29, 2020, which was during the height of pandemic restrictions. The hashtags like #workspace suggest this is their regular area for creating art, and hashtags like #liveyourbestlife and #fuckcovid19 suggest adaptation to pandemic conditions rather than temporary travel. Since the tweet originates from Austin and contains